WEBVTT

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.680
Can anyone see anything?

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.000
JESSIE: (GASPS)
There's a playground!

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.120
BUZZ: Wow!

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.240
We hit the jackpot, Bullseye!

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.360
HAMM: So much for sad
and lonely, huh?

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.680
Okay. Calm down, guys.
Let's just keep this in perspective.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.640
Perspective? This place is perfect.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.800
Woody, it's nice! See?
The door has a rainbow on it.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.120
(BUZZING DOOR OPEN)

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.360
-Hey there!
-BONNIE'S MOM: Wow!

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.000
Haven't seen you in ages.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.480
I just wanted to drop these old toys off.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.160
Is this Bonnie? Look how big you are.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.440
-BONNIE'S MOM: Say hi, sweetie.
-Hi.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.760
BONNIE'S MOM: Hey, how are
your kids? Molly and Andy?

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.080
ANDY'S MOM: Not kids anymore.
Andy's going to college on Friday.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:48.760
-BONNIE'S MOM: What?
-Can you believe it?

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:52.400
-You sure they won't miss these?
-No, they never get played with.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.920
-You see any kids?
-(GASPS) Where is she taking us?

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.560
(CHILDREN CHATTERING SOFTLY)

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:05.680
JESSIE: Look!
MR. POTATO HEAD: Wow!

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.400
What? What is it?

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.720
(BOTH ROARING)

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.160
No, no, no.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.320
What's the matter with you?

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.160
(EXCLAIMS) I can't see!

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:20.280
(BELL RINGING)

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.000
Okay, everyone. Recess. Come on!

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:23.520
CHILDREN: Yay!

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.520
HAMM: So now what do we do?
WOODY: We go back to Andy's.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.640
Anyone see an exit?

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.400
MR. POTATO HEAD: Exit, shmexit.
Let's get played with.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:34.920
BUZZ: Careful. These toys might be
jealous of new arrivals.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.160
-I want to see!
-HAMM: Hey!

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:37.400
-Rex!
-It's my turn!

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:44.560
New toys!

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:46.360
(ALL CHEERING)

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.720
Well, howdy! Glad to meet ya.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.640
Buzz Lightyear at your service.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:57.040
(CHUCKLES) Boy, oh, boy, oh, boy.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.440
(LAUGHING)

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.400
Oh. Thank you. May I?

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.680
Ooh! (LAUGHS)

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:07.920
The claw!

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:10.840
(TOY TRUCK HONKING)

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.880
Well, hello there.
I thought I heard new voices.

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.440
Welcome to Sunnyside, folks.
I'm Lots-o'-Huggin' Bear.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.000
But please call me Lotso.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.000
Buzz Lightyear. We come in...

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:29.120
(CHUCKLING)

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.080
First thing you gotta know about me,
I'm a hugger.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.040
Oh, look at you all. You've been
through a lot today, haven't ya?

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.800
Oh, it's been horrible.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.880
Well, you're safe now.
We're all castoffs here.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.440
We been dumped, donated,
yard-saled, secondhanded

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.840
and just plain thrown out.
But just you wait,

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:51.520
you'll find being donated was the
best thing that ever happened to ya.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:52.680
(WOODY SCOFFS)

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.960
Mr. Lotso, do toys here
get played with every day?

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.640
All day long. Five days a week.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.640
But what happens
when the kids grow up?

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.520
Well, now, I'll tell ya.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.840
When the kids get old,
new ones come in.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.400
When they get old,
new ones replace them.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:13.440
You'll never be outgrown or neglected,
never abandoned or forgotten.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.960
No owners means no heartbreak.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.480
Yee-haw!

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.000
-It's a miracle.
-And you wanted us to stay at Andy's.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:23.480
Because we're Andy's toys!

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:26.560
So you got donated by this Andy, huh?

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.600
Well, it's his loss, Sheriff.
He can't hurt you no more.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.800
-Whoa, whoa, no, no, no...
-Now, let's get you all settled in.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.160
Ken? Where is that boy?
Ken? New toys!

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.640
Far out! Down in a jiff, Lotso.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.920
So, who's ready for Ken's dream tour?

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:48.560
Let's show our new friends
where they'll be staying.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:50.080
Folks, if you want to step
right this way...

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:52.480
(DRAMATIC ROCK BALLAD PLAYING)

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.520
Hi, I'm Ken.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:04.280
Barbie. Have we ever met?

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.440
Uh-uh.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.440
-I would've remembered.
-(GIGGLES)

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:10.240
-Love your legwarmers.
-Nice ascot.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:13.320
Come on, Ken.
Recess don't last forever.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.360
Right on, Lotso. This way, everybody.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:16.560
(GIGGLING)

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:21.160
You got a lot to look forward to, folks.
The little ones love new toys.

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.760
-What a nice bear.
-And he smells like strawberries.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:25.880
(SIGHS)

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:29.040
Folks, if I can share,
here at Sunnyside, we've got,

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.960
well, just about anything
a toy could ask for.

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.840
Spare parts, superglue,

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:36.360
and enough fresh batteries
to choke a Hungry Hungry Hippo.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.680
-Think you're gettin' old?
-JESSIE: Wow.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.320
LOTSO: Well, stop your worryin'.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.160
KEN: Our repair spa will keep you
stuffed, puffed, and lightly buffed.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.840
(SNEEZES)

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:48.360
And this, well, this is where I live.

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:51.240
It's Ken's Dream House.
It has a disco, it's got a dune buggy.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:54.200
And a whole room
just for trying on clothes.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:55.320
(GASPS)

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.520
You have everything!

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:00.480
Everything except
someone to share it with.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:01.840
(GASPS)

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:06.800
You need anything at all,
you just come talk to me. Here we are.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.760
(GURGLES)

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:11.840
LOTSO: Well, thank you, Big Baby.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:15.040
Why don't you come meet
our new friends?

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.960
Poor baby. We were thrown out
together, me and him.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.200
Abandoned by the same owner.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:24.200
But we don't need owners
at Sunnyside.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:27.520
We own ourselves.
We're masters of our own fate.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.120
We control our own destiny.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.280
(EXCLAIMING)

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:31.720
Watch out for puddles.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.440
And here's where
you folks'll be stayin'.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:37.360
The Caterpillar Room.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.720
JESSIE: Look at this place.
MR. POTATO HEAD: Wow!

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.800
HAMM: Holy moly guacamole.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.400
MR. POTATO HEAD: Jackpot, baby.
(WHISTLES)

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.320
-Whoa, puppy!
-Hello.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:47.480
-Hello.
-Hello.

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:48.800
(TRAIN WHISTLE BLOWING)

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.240
It's so beautiful!

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.240
(TINKLING)

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:56.560
What the... Oh. Hey, little guy.

00:05:56.680 --> 00:05:59.080
How long's it been
since you all got played with?

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.200
It's been years.

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:04.480
Well, just you wait.
In a few minutes, that bell's gonna ring,

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:07.320
and you'll get the playtime
that you've been dreamin' of.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.320
Play! Real play! I can't wait!

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.240
Now, if you'll excuse us,
we best be headin' back.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:15.320
Welcome to Sunnyside, folks.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:16.480
-Thank you.
-Take care, pinky.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.160
-Goodbye, Mr. Lotso. Thank you.
-HAMM: Thank you, buddy boy.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:21.360
-Will I see you again?
-Oh, I'll see you tonight

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:22.920
in my dreams.

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:25.400
Ken, let's get a move on.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:27.840
Barbie, come with me.
Live in my dream house.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:31.680
I know it's crazy. I know we just met.
Heck, you don't know me from G.I. Joe,

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.840
but when I look at you,
I feel like we were...

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:35.120
-Made for each other.
-...made for each other.

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:36.280
(BOTH GASP)

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.040
-Yay!
-Yes.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.960
-LOTSO: Ken?
-Coming, Lotso.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.200
(BOTH GIGGLING)

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.040
BARBIE: This is so exciting!

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:47.080
(GURGLES)

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.520
(CHILDREN CHATTERING OUTSIDE)

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:52.880
HAMM: Sounds like kids to me.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:56.360
Oh, I want to get played with.
Why can't time go faster?

00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:57.960
How many you reckon are out there?

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.800
MRS. POTATO HEAD:
They sound so sweet.

